WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.937 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Unfortunately, my
experience in high school was,

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.206 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know not the best
because I had to race against

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
biological males my
entire high school career.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.610
I lost a lot of opportunities

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.479
because I lost four
state championships,

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:15.982 align:start position:0%
two Alumni awards, and countless
other opportunities to play

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.884
and advance and metals.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.693
- I'm Dave Rubin and
we're going to be doing

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.228
something a bit different today.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.929 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let me give you a
little backstory here

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.732
on May 22nd of this
year USA today put

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:84% position:16%
out an op-ed from
collegiate track star

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:39.139
Chelsea Mitchell about
her experiences competing

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.508
against transgender athletes.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.677
However, on May 25th,
just three days later

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:48.314
the publication changed the
word male to transgender

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:84% position:16%
throughout her piece,
without warning

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
and called her out for using
quote "Hurtful language."

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.791
In an editor's note,
the outlet explained

00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:02.429
that the op-ed was updated to
"Reflect USA today's standards

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.164
and style guidelines.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:07.567 align:start size:84% position:16%
We regret that hurtful
language was used."

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.703 align:start size:88% position:13%
Today I'm speaking
with the author of that

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.172
op-ed and her lawyer

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:97% position:3%
please welcome one of the
fastest girls in Connecticut.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:88% position:13%
Track star Chelsea
Mitchell and her lawyer

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.612
who is the general counsel

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.815 align:start size:81% position:19%
at the Alliance
defending freedom.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:97% position:3%
Kristin Wagoner, ladies,
welcome to the Rubin report.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.419
- Thank you.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.720
- Thank you.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.955
- All right.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.257
So I'm glad to have
both of you, Kristen.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.394 align:start position:0%
I reached out to you originally
when I saw this story

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
on Twitter, because
it just so fit

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.765
so many of the things
that I've been talking

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.601
about on this show,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.103
Chelsea I'll

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'll start with you since
you wrote the original piece.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, I guess first
just tell me how you got

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.910
into track and, and, and
you enjoy running, right?

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.378 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like that's really
what this is all about.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to compete
against girls in running?

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.917 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah. I was an
athlete my entire life.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I got to high school,
I started running track

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:04.124
and I kind of quickly realized
that I was really good at it.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.659
And unfortunately my experience

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.228
in high school was,

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:11.331
you know not the best
because I had to race

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.832
against, biological males

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.267
my entire high school career.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
I lost a lot of
opportunities because of them

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.604
I lost four state

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:81% position:19%
championships,
two alumni awards,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.341
and countless other
opportunities to play

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.909
and advance and metals.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Right. So when did it
start that biological boys

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:31.684
trans girls were in the
races that you were in?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.153
In girls races.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:37.056
- Yeah, my freshman year was
when it first started happening

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.791
- And, and was it immediate that

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.593
they were audit like right out

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:97% position:3%
of the gate, they were faster
and winning all the races

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.431
- Right out the gate.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.734
They were still placing
very high in the state.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, when I was a
freshman, I placed seventh

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.672
at the state open in
the a hundred meters

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:55.875 align:start position:0%
and one of the biological males
comes in third knocking me

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:59.746
out of the spot to advance in
the New Zealand championship.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:03.550
- Right. So so what caused
you to write this piece?

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.052 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then I'll get to sort
of where the, the legal part

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this is, and then we'll
get Kristen involved.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.190
- I really just wanted
to bring attention to

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:88% position:13%
what has been happening
in Connecticut

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I personally think
it's really unfair to

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.962
have biological males raced

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.264 align:start size:88% position:13%
against biological
females because we just

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.301 align:start position:0%
cannot keep up with the physical
advantages of a male body.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.037
And so I decided to put
out my own story out

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:26.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
there so that people
could understand what was

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.974
happening and how unfair it was.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.011 align:start position:0%
- And to be clear, I'm
guessing you are not anti-trans

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.946
in any way?

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.780
- No not at all.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.281
- Put it out there.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.983
Okay. So, so Kristin

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.752 align:start size:88% position:13%
when did you get
involved in all of this?

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.922 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, initially
we filed a complaint

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.624
with the department
of education that was

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.527 align:start position:0%
during the Trump
administration in June of 2019.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.762
And as time continued to pass

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we weren't
seeing the department

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.467 align:start size:84% position:16%
of ed take substantive
action on it.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:58.771 align:start size:97% position:3%
We ended up filing a
lawsuit in February of 2020

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.840 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that was
Chelsea senior year.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.775 align:start size:81% position:19%
And there were
some circumstances

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.712
for her where she was ready
to move forward with that.

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.580
And we were glad to assist

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.550
because there were four
state championship titles

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:84% position:16%
that she was losing
and it was just coming

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the end where we needed
to get judicial relief.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.224
And so that's why we
filed the lawsuit.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.959
- Right? So Chelsea

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.829
what are most people think
sort of behind the scenes?

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:26.266
I, I sense that there's sort
of an activist class and a

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:29.302 align:start size:88% position:13%
a media class that loves
pushing these stories

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:32.138
but the average person that's
going to these track events

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.475
and watching you lose to
a biological male probably

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.944
gets why you're
upset about this.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.747 align:start position:0%
- Yeah. I think a lot of people
who have seen this happen

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:43.783
in Connecticut understand
how unfair it is especially

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:47.920 align:start size:97% position:3%
because these biological males
were beating us females by

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.524
significant margins in these
races, and it was happening

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:55.128
at every single race we raced
against them, we were losing.

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:58.831 align:start position:0%
And it was a big difference
and everyone can tell you that.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:02.335
- Yeah. So, so Kristen,
what do you want legally?

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.936
What, what would be right for

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.772
to legally happen at this point

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Well there are four
girls that are in the case

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.411
in Connecticut, two

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.413
who graduated and two remain
in the Connecticut schools.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.615
And so for the two
that have graduated

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.583 align:start size:84% position:16%
including Chelsea
and also Selena Soule

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:21.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
those records need to be
corrected in this case alone

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:23.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's important to realize
there were two boys

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.991
that identified as girls.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of those boys competed
as a girl three weeks

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:31.564
before he decided to move
over and compete as a girl.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:35.068 align:start size:88% position:13%
And those two boys
took 15 different races

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:38.071
championships away from girls
during those three seasons.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
So there was a huge
impact in Connecticut.

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.142 align:start size:84% position:16%
So we want the records
to be set straight.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then for the girls
that are continuing

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.813
and in this Connecticut system

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:49.115
they need to be assured
that they're going to

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
be biological girls
competing against each other.

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.419
And

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.321
that it's going to be a fair
playing field moving forward.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.657
- I suspect I know the
answer to this question

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.692
but is there any evidence

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:04.130 align:start size:88% position:13%
of biological girls
transitioning to be boys

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.065
and then winning in boys sports?

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.636
- I, I none that
I can think of any

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:13.206 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm sure there may be isolated
cases where that's true

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.642
but what we do know is
that when boys transition

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:20.146
into the girl sports, there are
hundreds, literally hundreds

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.814 align:start size:84% position:16%
of high school boys
that can beat the most

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:24.183
elite female runners

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:27.153
and they have a 10 to
50% performance gap.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when you're just
looking at averages alone

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:33.192 align:start size:88% position:13%
immediate mediocre male
athlete will almost

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:36.262
always be able to be an
elite female athlete.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:39.665
- Now Chelsea, if I was to
repeat what Chris had just

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.100
said right there

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.835 align:start position:0%
somebody would say you're being
transphobic boys and girls

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.804
men and women are
exactly the same.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:48.474
Do you concede that there are
some biological differences?

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:50.810
- Of course there are
biological difference

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.678
between males and females.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.781
That's why we have
sex separated sports.

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.982
I mean, you know

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.718 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's kind of hard to
just put biological male

00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:01.053
female category
and say that it's

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:05.224
not an issue when
I know so many boys

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:06.359
in the state

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:07.693
could easily beat me

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.296
and they would not win
the state championship

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:12.131
if they were in
the boy category.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.634 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right. So what
would you prefer that

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:17.270
that those trans athletes do

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.272
should they have their
own division altogether

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:22.442 align:start size:97% position:3%
or you would just prefer
that, okay, you were born male

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:25.411 align:start size:97% position:3%
you should just be competing
with the, with the boys

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.480
regardless of how you
feel about yourself.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.681
Something like that.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.583
- I think the most
important thing is to

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:33.619 align:start size:84% position:16%
protect the female
category and make sure

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
that us females are
having a fair competition.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.693
And I think that should be
the number one priority.

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.429
- Right? Kristen, what'd
you make of a USA today

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:45.364
switching some of
the language here.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:48.067
I mean, once you submit an
op-ed, you know, I, you know

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.503
Chelsea wrote a piece that
was honest and heartfelt

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:52.205
and then suddenly it's not just

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:53.606
that they're changing language.

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.041
The implication is somehow

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:58.511 align:start size:97% position:3%
that what Chelsea was
saying was somehow hateful.

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.379
- It was shocking to us.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.316
I mean, we, we write
op-eds all the time.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:06.319
Our clients are writing
op-eds and we can't think

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:09.489
of any other instance
in the 30 year history

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:12.024 align:start size:84% position:16%
we've been involved
in public interest law

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.893
where they have felt

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.995
like they could change
what someone else wrote

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.497
without even advanced notice.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.131
Like, we didn't get
a call that said, Hey

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.334
just want you to know
this just happened.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.836 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's just, it's shocking
in terms of the lack

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:26.839
of journalistic integrity,
and also the accusations

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:29.108
because nothing could be
further from the truth.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:30.576
- Right? Well, is there any

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:33.379 align:start position:0%
is there any legal recourse
you can take with them on that?

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.882
I mean, the idea that they
changed it three days later

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:38.718
implying that somehow
the policy changed as

00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:40.820 align:start size:84% position:16%
if they didn't read
it in the first place.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:43.990
- There probably is, but
I don't know that we're

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.525
as interested in
that is making sure

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:48.394 align:start position:0%
that the public knows that
this language isn't appropriate

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:52.231
that what USA has done is USA
today has done isn't right.

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.400
And winning this
case for our girls

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.969 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean girls should
have equal opportunities

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:59.438
the same opportunities
that their brothers have

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.541
and they need to be
authentic and real.

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:04.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that can't happen
when male bodied athletes

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.813
are competing in
the girls category.

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:09.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Chelsea, can you
just talk a little bit

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:11.217
about what it's like to
be a young person going

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:14.654
through the mob and the,
and the monster that so

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:16.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
many people fear that
that's really why I reached

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:19.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
out to Kristen originally
when I saw this

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:20.560
because I just saw, oh

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.828
here's just a nice
girl who wants to run

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:24.897
and tell her story, that's it.

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:28.067
And then of course you read
the stuff that they're saying

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.736 align:start position:0%
about you and about you
Kristin, and all the rest of it.

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:33.506 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's just, it's just
nothing to do with the truth.

00:09:34.941 --> 00:09:36.409
- It's really frustrating
especially because this

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:39.412
is just about the boys, you
know the biology matters

00:09:39.412 --> 00:09:41.814
in sports and I think that
t's really obvious to a lot

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:44.317
of people so you know I'm
not trying to be harmful

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:47.653
in any way, I just want
to be able to run on a

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:49.088
fair playing field.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:51.490 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah. But what about
getting all the mean tweets?

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:52.725
Not fun, right?

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:55.561 align:start size:84% position:16%
- No, but you know,
you always got to look

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:58.531
at the support instead
of all the mean tweets.

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:00.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah. Kristen,
are you seeing this?

00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:02.101
You guys are in Connecticut

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:04.070 align:start size:97% position:3%
but are you seeing this
like all across the country?

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:07.974
There's so many cases that
sounds so similar to this.

00:10:07.974 --> 00:10:10.509 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Absolutely. We
have a case in Idaho.

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:13.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, it is, you've probably
seen, there've been 30

00:10:13.379 --> 00:10:15.548 align:start size:88% position:13%
some different state
proposals that were just

00:10:15.548 --> 00:10:16.983
proposed this last year

00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:19.085 align:start position:0%
because we are seeing it happen
across the United States.

00:10:19.085 --> 00:10:20.853
I've seen it on my
own daughter's teams

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:24.490 align:start size:88% position:13%
in conservative Arizona
softball as well a

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.424
soccer we've had

00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:27.727
volleyball teams that have

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:29.695
called us where literally
a girl got a concussion

00:10:29.695 --> 00:10:32.131 align:start size:84% position:16%
from being hit
with a guy playing.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:34.567 align:start size:84% position:16%
And, and of course
they're playing on
the lower nets, right?

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:36.569
And then we have the Idaho case

00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:39.372 align:start size:88% position:13%
which where the ACLU
immediately brought suit

00:10:39.372 --> 00:10:42.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
challenging a law that
protected women in that state.

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:44.510
And they're trying
to get it struck

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:45.778
down at the night circuit.

00:10:45.778 --> 00:10:47.613
And we represent
two track athletes

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:49.715
at the collegiate level
in that case as well.

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:51.484 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I'm actually glad that
you brought that case

00:10:51.484 --> 00:10:52.918 align:start size:84% position:16%
up because I was going
to bring that up.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:55.688
But what has happened to
the ACLU that was once

00:10:55.688 --> 00:10:59.492 align:start size:97% position:3%
the great defender of civil
liberties in the United States

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.928 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now is, is actually
attacking women in essence.

00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:05.297
- It's horrific.

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:07.700
I mean, it's just so stunning
when you think about the fact

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.202
that the ACLU would go after,
you know, with defend those

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:14.407
in Skokie so many years ago,
and yet on free speech matters

00:11:14.407 --> 00:11:16.208
they don't believe in
free speech anymore.

00:11:16.208 --> 00:11:18.411
And we used to be able
to say that, you know

00:11:18.411 --> 00:11:21.147
we would defend
to the death, you

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:24.517
for your free speech rights,
even if we disagree with you.

00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:26.152
And that used to be
the ACLU's position

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:29.422 align:start size:97% position:3%
but they've abandoned it long
ago in favor of ideology.

00:11:29.422 --> 00:11:30.956
I will say though

00:11:30.956 --> 00:11:34.060 align:start size:88% position:13%
that there is a broader
coalition that's
supporting Chelsea.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.362 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this issue,
there are, you know

00:11:36.362 --> 00:11:38.898
feminists that are coming out
and saying, this is not right.

00:11:38.898 --> 00:11:40.266
And we're thankful for them.

00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:42.768
We might not align with
them on other issues.

00:11:42.768 --> 00:11:45.705
But man, where we do align
is that biology matters.

00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:47.807 align:start size:81% position:19%
And that we're
setting women back

00:11:47.807 --> 00:11:50.543
by allowing men to
call themselves women

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:53.979
and compete against women
in their own categories.

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:57.249 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Chelsea, I can sense you're,
you're wired sort of cool

00:11:57.249 --> 00:11:59.518
which I like here, but
can you talk a little bit

00:11:59.518 --> 00:12:02.154
