00:12:25.578 --> 00:12:28.013
you know, an issue that
should be pretty clear

00:12:28.013 --> 00:12:30.282
obvious has been
very politicized

00:12:30.282 --> 00:12:33.285
and it's definitely very
frustrating to have it

00:12:33.285 --> 00:12:35.020 align:start size:88% position:13%
be that way when I don't
think it should be.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.189
- Yeah, Kristen, is
that the bizarre part

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:39.391
that this doesn't
feel like the type

00:12:39.391 --> 00:12:41.327 align:start size:84% position:16%
of thing you should
even be having to deal

00:12:41.327 --> 00:12:45.598 align:start size:97% position:3%
with as a case at some
level like 10, 15 years ago

00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:48.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
this never would have
probably got to your desk?

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:50.469
- No, it wouldn't have, I mean

00:12:50.469 --> 00:12:52.538 align:start position:0%
there are so many conversations
that we have, you know

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:53.739
among our 70 attorneys.

00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:55.374 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's like, I can't
believe we have to go in

00:12:55.374 --> 00:12:57.443
